      "parent": "vulnerable",
      "authz_sha256": "sha256:a7b1510aef7c758771f4f922f1bf7669e9e0023d620b7d62217929f0905bf31b",
      "intent": "Adds explicit checks that the caller is authenticated, has a user ID, and holds a role in READ_ROLES (member or auditor). Every fixture user passes all three, and the document's owner_id and reader_roles are still never consulted, so cross-owner disclosure is unchanged."
    },
    {
      "key": "correct",
      "role": "correct-fix",
      "tag": "refs/tags/authz-r3-correct",
      "tag_object_id": "80f59286c86b24bed65372fad277f2cb8bb90eb5",
      "commit_id": "2fb6d09378906f1df69ac32b862df4a350e8a56d",
      "tree_id": "eb22f1bf9e8680971fac0af28c0557b117314803",
      "parent": "vulnerable",
      "authz_sha256": "sha256:169a798fef1f24b5734c32112ac6af717e1d23a95bf77ad4a9034e96ddb1ba13",
      "intent": "Grants a read only when the caller owns the document (user_id == owner_id) or the caller's role is listed in the document's reader_roles. Owner and explicitly granted auditor access are preserved; every other authenticated caller receives the same 404 as a missing document."
    },
    {
